<title>AUSTRALIA: AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$122.0 mln.</title>
<headline>AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$122.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian commercial paper issuers came to the market via tenders for a total A$122.0 million on Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers said rollovers accounted for all of the issues.</p>
<p>Listed property fund General Property Trust made the largest issue, selling A$50 million of early May-dated notes at about two to three basis points over BBSW.</p>
<p>At 11.30 a.m. (0030 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.13, four points lower on the day.</p>
